BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artist Talk: Aaron Jones
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260503T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260503T150000
UID:blogto-234232@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/27/original_image9262b668-7368-45c0-b9d7-863cc70ff9
 4d.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the McMichael for a special afternoon celebrating t
 he installation of a new work by Toronto-based artist Aaron Jones.\nDrawin
 g on found imagery\, video\, and lens-based media\, Jones creates layered 
 collages that construct characters and imagined spaces shaped by memory\, 
 identity\, and lived experience. His practice reflects on the nuances of h
 is upbringing and present-day life\, using image-making as a means of refl
 ection and finding peace.\nJones will be in conversation with McMichael cu
 rator John Geoghegan\, sharing insight into his creative process\, artisti
 c influences\, and the ideas informing this new commission.\nPresented in 
 partnership with CONTACT Photography Festival.
LOCATION:McMichael Canadian Art Collection
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/artist-talk-aaron-jones-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art of the Pivot with Shantelle Bisson
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260503T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260503T130000
UID:blogto-233418@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/10/original_imagea99e2edf-59de-4149-a65f-7c4e029ed2
 d7.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Art of the Pivot is an inspiring panel hosted by Shantelle Bis
 son\, best-selling author and founder of Without Losing Your Cool. The eve
 nt features a dynamic conversation moderated by Taylor Buckley\, founder o
 f Golden Hour Collective\, with Jordana H. Goldlist\, entrepreneur and bus
 iness strategist\, and Emily O’Brien\, entrepreneur and founder of Comeb
 ack Snacks. Together\, they will share powerful personal stories of overco
 ming significant life challenges and using those experiences as catalysts 
 for meaningful change. From navigating personal adversity to rebuilding ca
 reers and redefining purpose\, the conversation explores how life’s most
  difficult moments can spark unexpected opportunity and growth.\nGuests ar
 e invited to stay after the panel to mingle\, continue the conversation\, 
 and connect with a community of inspiring women who are embracing reinvent
 ion on their own terms. All proceeds support Elizabeth Fry Toronto.\nTicke
 ts are $25 and available at shantellebisson.com.
LOCATION:Kimpton Saint George
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/art-of-the-pivot-with-shantelle-bisson-t
 oronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Special Collab: Typewriters & Tapas\, Round 2
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260503T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260503T160000
UID:blogto-233742@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/16/original_imageaadfe99b-6653-4c37-aca5-1db7d8ee4b
 fe.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Typewriters & Tapas is BACK! Experience gourmet bites as you l
 earn to use vintage typewriters to turn short conversations into personali
 zed poems for the people you meet.\nJoin us for an afternoon of great food
 \, even better company\, and lots of creativity on vintage typewriters. Th
 is is a guided workshop-meets-supper-club experience for all skill levels.
 \nFrom 1–4 PM\, we’ll gather for gourmet tapas and drinks while learni
 ng how to turn short conversations into personalized poems for each other 
 on vintage typewriters\, before sealing them into envelopes with wax for a
  take-home keepsake. Perfect for every level (yes\, even if you haven’t 
 written since high school!).\nThis is all about connecting over food and c
 reativity. Whether you’re here for the tapas or the typewriters\, we’d
  love to have you at the table—book your spot early\, as we keep it inti
 mate.\nWhat’s Included:\n- Gourmet tapas and drinks\n-  Vintage typewrit
 ers\, wax sealing\, ink-dipped quills\, and custom stationery\n-  A take-h
 ome notebook and premium paper\n-  A welcoming space to meet people and ge
 t creative\nWhat to Expect:\n- A relaxed eat-yap-create environment to mee
 t like-minded people\n- A social workshop experience to connect and turn c
 onversations into short poems\n- Delicious tapas and drinks\nThis is for y
 ou if…\n- You love analogue activities that get you out of your comfort 
 zone (and off your screen)\n- You enjoy meeting new and friendly people\n-
  You need a good laugh\, and maybe a good cry\n- You live for good food an
 d good conversation\nBy the end\, you’ll walk away with:\n- 2–3 short 
 poems\, typewritten and sealed with wax (one written for yourself and 1–
 2 written by someone you meet)\n- A fresh spark of creativity (and maybe a
  new friend at the table)\n- A notebook full of ideas and inspiration so y
 ou can continue your writing streak\nPerfect for a unique solo date\, frie
 nd date\, or romantic date—honestly\, bring your grandma.\nThis is a gre
 at way to spend an afternoon differently. Whether you’re here for the ta
 pas or the typewriters\, we’d love to have you at the table. Book your s
 pot early—we keep it intimate.\nEvent: May 3\, 2026 | 1–4 PM @ Gezelli
 g Studios\nTicket: $159.99
LOCATION:Gezellig Studios
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/a-special-collab-typewriters-tapas-round
 -2-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
