 bd.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Sport Inspiring Meaningful Cultural Exchange\nThe Annual Eva H
 oltby Lecture on Contemporary Culture brings the world’s most sought-aft
 er and thought-provoking voices to ROM for compelling conversations that
  spark curiosity and challenge perspectives. Since 2006\, this highly cele
 brated series has explored the ways art and culture shape who we are and h
 ow we see the world.\nThis year\, two Canadian soccer superstars take the 
 stage to explore sport as a powerful force for international cultural dipl
 omacy\, transcending political and social boundaries to build unity\, mutu
 al understanding\, and national pride. From grassroots initiatives strengt
 hening local communities to world-renowned athletes advocating for social 
 change\, and global events like the World Cup\, this dynamic talk aims to 
 reveal how sport can inspire dialogue\, connection\, and meaningful cultur
 al exchange.\nMember Price: $36.00\nRegular Price: $40.00
LOCATION:Royal Ontario Museum
