BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Night School Lecture and Social - Microdosing... What do we know a
 nd how confident are we about it?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260506T184500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260506T210000
UID:blogto-234462@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/30/original_image1b885222-c4d3-4753-b939-dcbb50a951
 da.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Microdosing is popular\, but is it proven? A live Night School
  on psychedelics\, evidence\, and the limits of what we know.\nNight Schoo
 l Lecture + Social: Where Scholarship Meets Cultural Life\nMicrodosing psy
 chedelics is everywhere\, but how much of it is actually backed by science
 ?\nFor this Night School\, we’re joined by Rotem Petranker\, Director of
  the Canadian Centre for Psychedelic Science and researcher behind the wor
 ld’s largest randomized controlled trial on psilocybin microdosing for d
 epression.\nThis isn’t a hype talk.\nIt’s a clear look at the quality 
 of the evidence and how confident we should really be in it.\nWhat you’l
 l experience:\nPart lecture\, part real conversation.\nRotem will break do
 wn what microdosing is\, why it’s become so popular\, and what happens w
 hen you actually test it under controlled conditions.\nYou’ll get a rare
  look at how this research is done and what the latest findings do (and do
 n’t) show.\nWhat we’ll get into:\n• What microdosing is (and isn’t
 )\n• Why the current evidence is still considered weak\n• Inside the w
 orld’s largest psilocybin microdosing trial for depression\n• Placebo\
 , expectation\, and perception\n• Why this field is so difficult to stud
 y\n• The key question: what is the minimum viable dose that actually doe
 s something?\nThe core idea:\nWe know that large doses have measurable eff
 ects.\nThe real question is how little might actually matter?\nWho this is
  for:\nPeople who are curious about the mind\, skeptical of trends\, and i
 nterested in what the evidence actually says.\nNo background needed\, just
  curiosity.\nAbout the Speaker:\nRotem Petranker is Director of the Canadi
 an Centre for Psychedelic Science and co-founder of the Psychedelic Studie
 s Research Program at the University of Toronto.\nHe led the world’s lar
 gest randomized controlled trial on psilocybin microdosing for Major Depre
 ssive Disorder\, bringing clinical rigor to one of the most talked-about t
 opics in mental health.\nHis work explores psychedelics\, attention\, and 
 how we understand subjective experience.\nAbout Night School:\nNight Schoo
 l is a live lecture series designed to feel more like a great night out th
 an a classroom.\nWe bring researchers\, thinkers\, and storytellers into i
 ntimate spaces for talks that are engaging\, social\, and actually worth y
 our time.\nThink: big ideas with a drink in hand.
LOCATION:Night School Toronto
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/night-school-lecture-and-social-microdos
 ing-what-do-we-know-and-how-confident-are-we-about-it-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
