BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:'Photo Diary' Exhibition - Karolina Kuras & Ted Belton
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260507T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260508T170000
UID:blogto-233505@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/12/original_imagedc724e0c-42c0-4e1e-871f-a7dc11d132
 1b.jpg
DESCRIPTION:On May 2026\, Album Studios and CONTACT Photography Festival p
 resent "Photo Diary"\, an exhibition that intertwines the compelling works
  of Karolina Kuras' ballet photography and Ted Belton's fashion photograph
 y.\nBoth with special eyes for movement\, texture\, and contrast\, their w
 ork creates windows into the souls of their subjects\, and the auras under
 neath honest moments better translated visually than with words. Their con
 temporary styles naturally complement each other\, capturing discipline an
 d grace in visual conversation. Together\, their photographs reveal how fa
 shion and dance are connected practices\, through their vulnerable yet per
 formative natures. This exhibition is a "Photo Diary" of Karolina and Ted
 ’s photography practices\, experimenting with human expression\, creativ
 e process\, and print materials.\nAbout the Artists:\nKarolina Kuras is a 
 Toronto based ballet and portrait photographer. Internationally recognized
  as one of the foremost photographers working in ballet today\, she works 
 at the intersection of classical ballet and fashion\, producing images tha
 t are precise\, elegant\, and entirely her own. A classically trained danc
 er herself\, Karolina brings an embodied understanding of movement and lin
 e to every shoot. On set she directs and shapes movement specifically for 
 the camera\, ensuring each image is intentional rather than incidental. Ha
 ving worked with some of the most celebrated ballet companies in the world
 \, her work is built on the trust of the people she photographs and a deep
  respect and understanding for the art form.\nTed Belton is a Canadian pho
 tographer living in Toronto and working internationally. His fashion pictu
 res and portraits have appeared in titles such as AirMail\, Dazed\, Kinfol
 k\, and Rolling Stone. Ted’s interest in documenting individuals of exce
 ptional character and style has brought him to the streets of Paris\, into
  the homes of eccentrics and socialites\, the studios of artists\, musicia
 ns\, and designers\, and to skate parks and fashion weeks around the world
 . Wherever he is\, Ted’s eye remains tuned to the quiet qualities of his
  subjects that he aims to amplify into memorable statements.\nAbout The Ve
 nue:\nAlbum Studios is a Toronto-based studio rental space for film produc
 tion\, photographers\, and events. We offer 7 studio spaces across 3 locat
 ions in West Toronto - Geary Avenue\, The Junction\, and Mount Dennis.\nEx
 hibition Details:\nTitle: Photo Diary\nArtists: Karolina Kuras and Ted Bel
 ton\nDates: May 7 - May 31\, 2026\nLocation: Album Studios\nAddress: 92 Ge
 ary Ave\, Toronto\nOpening Reception: Thurs\, May 7\, 2026 / 6:00 - 11:00 
 PM / Refreshments will be served.\nGallery Viewing: Thurs\, May 7 until Su
 n\, May 31 / 8:00 AM - 5:00 PM\nAdmission is free.\nEvent Registration: ht
 tps://luma.com/se9yuygd\nContact: events@albumstudios.com | https://www.al
 bumstudios.com/contactfest2026
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/photo-diary-exhibition-karolina-kuras-te
 d-belton-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pints & Puzzles at Left Field Brewery in Leslieville Toronto
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260507T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260507T210000
UID:blogto-234207@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
