 ries testing you on pop culture's best and brightest celebs\, tv\, movies\
 , music\, and so much more!\nInteractive games mixed throughout testing yo
 ur agility and wit for BONUS points!\nSpecials\n$10 Guinness! Attempt to S
 plit the G for 1 PT. Successfully split the G for 5 Pts! (1 / Table)\nWHO 
 SHOULD ATTEND\nThink trivia isn’t your thing? Perfect – this is exactl
 y for you.\nAt Question Everything Trivia\, we flip the script on your ave
 rage game night. Forget boring\, brain-busting questions and awkward silen
 ces – this is trivia reimagined. Expect laughs\, sass\, and pop-culture 
 madness that keeps everyone engaged\, whether you know the answers or not.
 \nWe’re inclusive\, welcoming\, and all about good vibes.\nPRIZES\nA $50
  Fortunate Fox gift card for 1st place winners!\n1 Hour GRETA Unlimited Pl
 ay Passes!\n* Additional prizes change on a week-to-week basis\, and are d
 ependent on weekly sponsors and attendance.\nVENUE & TICKET RULES\nPlease 
 arrive as close to 6:45 as possible to be seated so that the game can star
 t promptly at 7PM\nOnce tickets are sold out\, please join waitlist to be 
 the first to know if someone releases their spot last minute.\n$25 Minimum
  Spend / Person. This is just a couple drinks and food so it shouldn't be 
 hard to reach\, and helps the bar continue to provide these nights and epi
 c prizes!\nFor groups of 6 people or more\, a 20% gratuity will be automat
 ically added to your bill on the day.\n***IMPORTANT: RSVPS ARE NOT GUARANT
 EED SEATING***\nRSVPing does not reserve you a spot or table! It is just t
 o notify us and the restaurant that people are attending.\nThe restaurant 
 has limited seating capacity\, so to guarentee your group a spot\, arrive 
 early! Sitting is all first come first serve.\nPlease make sure you get to
  get there early to get the best possible spot. An RSVP is not a guarantee
 \, it's dependant on space. We simply use RSVPs to gauge how many people t
 o expect\, but of course as it's a free event\, we sometimes have no-shows
 . We do what we can to accomodate everyone who RSVPs. If you are concerned
  about making the trip\, you can reach out directly to double check about 
 seating\, and secure a reservation!
