BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Carabao\, Mayworks
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260508T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260508T210000
UID:blogto-233893@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/20/original_imagefd71d188-28bc-4e27-8953-677ee8c936
 b0.jpg
DESCRIPTION:By Roann Enriquez\, developed through Mayworks’ Labour Art C
 atalyst in partnership with Anakbayan Toronto\, and informed by research i
 nterviews conducted with Migrante Ontario\, presented in collaboration wit
 h Tarragon Theatre.\nCarabao is a play in development depicting the trials
  and tribulations of a Filipino family across borders\, from Manila and Ca
 buyao City to Toronto and Thunder Bay. Inspired by the historic 74-hour st
 rike at Nexperia Philippines Inc. in March 2025\, the play also addresses 
 illegal recruitment and labour trafficking of Filipino migrant workers int
 o Canada – commonly practiced by unscrupulous agencies amidst rising ant
 i-immigration sentiments around the world. This work of issue-based theatr
 e allows audiences to reflect on the contributions of everyday Filipinos i
 n the workplace – from Chinese-owned manufacturing facilities to Canada
 ’s long-term care homes – as well as on the power of collective action
  in the global labour struggle for workers.\nThe script will be workshoppe
 d with a director and actors over two days. A final read through will be o
 pen to the public at the end of each day\, followed by a Q&A with the play
 wright and Anakbayan Toronto.\nRegister at mayworks.ca\nThis venue is whee
 lchair accessible and has gender neutral\, wheelchair accessible washrooms
 .
LOCATION:Tarragon Theatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/carabao-mayworks-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cup for Cup 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260508T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260508T140000
UID:blogto-234455@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/30/original_image8a0bce0f-caa5-40fc-8f00-10872a3b53
 e6.jpg
DESCRIPTION:We are excited to invite you and your friends/ team to our 2nd
  Annual Cup for Cup on Friday May 8\, 2026\,  at The Old Spaghetti Factory
 \, downtown Toronto in support of Safe Water Social Ventures’ (SWSV) ann
 ual fundraising event which provides safe drinking water to communities in
  need. This fundraising event is hosted by The Old Spaghetti Factory in do
 wntown Toronto.\nCup For Cup is an innovative initiative of Safe Water Soc
 ial Ventures (SWSV) that encourages water users such as factories\, restau
 rants\, households etc. to replenish the equivalent amount of water they u
 se or consume by providing an equivalent amount of safe water to families 
 in need. This enables them to provide sustainable and locally manufactured
  bio-sand water purifiers to families in need in Uganda\, East Africa\, wh
 ere water-borne diseases prevail as a result of contaminated water sources
 .\nLast year\, 22 families received bio-sand water filters thanks to funds
  raised during Cup for Cup 2025. These filters last for about 25 years and
  save families about $40.00 in medical expenses each year. This amount mig
 ht seem relatively small to us\, but it is a lot to a family that lives on
  less than $3.00 per day.\n\nFor every lunch entrée purchased at the down
 town Toronto restaurant during Cup for Cup on May 8\, 2026\, The Old Spagh
 etti Factory will generously donate $10 to support SWSV’s safe drinking 
 water projects in East Africa. In addition\, certain members of The Old Sp
 aghetti Factory’s food and beverage suppliers have committed to offsetti
 ng the water used in their production by helping more families with locall
 y made bio-sand water purifiers.\nYou and your team/ guests can participat
 e simply by ordering from the designated menu items knowing your meal will
  make a difference in people’s lives.\nCheck out the Old Spaghetti Facto
 ry Toronto’s video about this project:\nhttps://lnkd.in/eAdmfG_P\nCheck 
 out the 2-minute video on the SWSV Cup For Cup program:\nhttps://lnkd.in/e
 3vE3DTq\nLearn more and register ahead for FREE to let us know you're comi
 ng!  Or if you would like a table for your colleagues or customers\, we ar
 e happy to reserve an entire table.\nEvent info and sign-up page link here
 : https://lnkd.in/exxZKaXr\nWe look forward to hosting you and your team b
 etween 11:30am and 2:00pm on May 8 2026\, at The Old Spaghetti Factory in 
 downtown Toronto.\nCome and network with fellow supporters and let us make
  a meaningful impact together while sharing pasta with purpose.
LOCATION:The Old Spaghetti Factory\, downtown Toronto
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/cup-for-cup-2026-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
