 d international bands and DJs playing high-energy global beats to keep the
  dance floor moving late into the night.\nDeparture Festival presents this
  week's showcase\, bringing you the most electrifying emerging talent on t
 he planet.\nLexxicon\nLexxicon isn’t asking dancehall to evolve\, he’s
  dragging it into the future. Pastor’s kid turned Queer Dancehall Disrup
 tor\, he overloads the genre’s bounce with Brazilian Funk\, Dembow and R
 eggaeton\, building sleek volatile tracks that explode with confidence.\nW
 ith Jamaican roots\, Toronto grit\, and a global club vision He’s widely
  recognized as a pioneer for openly queer voices in reggae/dancehall a lin
 e in the sand he drew with album “Pink Fraternity” and doubles down on
  with “Slackness”.\nDJ Uncle Debo\nUncle Debo is an open format Dj and
  music lover. He enjoys playing Afrobeats\, Amapiano\, R&B and the likes. 
 He expresses himself with his music choice and mic work so come ready to h
 it the Dancefloor.\nArrive at 11 pm and enjoy some of the Latin orchestra 
 before the late-night global party begins!\nTickets\n$15 Early Bird\n$20 A
 dvance\nFree entry with Departure Pass\nBottle Service\nReservations for b
 ottle service can be made by calling 416 588 0307.\nPlease note that these
  tickets are general admission and do not guarantee seating. Buy early and
  get the early bird discount!
