BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Music Gallery presents What Is: noncompliance Night 3: No memo
 ries available
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260508T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260508T220000
UID:blogto-233849@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/19/original_image9d2b91a9-15d1-4d30-909e-d47c248b8b
 ca.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Calling our bodies to the front\, this night of performance su
 bverts power and authority over our form.\nOn our third night of What Is: 
 noncompliance\, we call our bodies to the practice. Our connection to the 
 body is not a given\, this is a reminder of everything we are and are capa
 ble of.\n1. THE PERFORMANCE at 8PM: Aliyah Aziz\, joined by her workshop p
 artners\, opens the night with a musical piece dedicated to unraveling tap
 e loops that bring memory back to tangibility. Following Aliyah is Qiujian
 g Levi Lu who uses their own electroacoustic systems to play and extend th
 e body into a transgressive and transhumanist locus. They cultivate discov
 ery and awareness in the queerness\, viscerality\, indecency and misconduc
 t of our bodies.\n2. THE ACTIVATION: Artist Husna Farooqui compiles a reso
 urce list centred around noncompliance in music to accompany the performan
 ces of the night.\nPWYCA $20\, $25\, $30\nTickets - https://www.showpass.c
 om/no-memories-available/\nFest Pass - https://www.showpass.com/what-is-no
 ncompliance-fest-pass/
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/the-music-gallery-presents-what-is-nonco
 mpliance-night-3-no-memories-available-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Ordinary Markup Marche Pop Up
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260508T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260508T190000
UID:blogto-234283@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/28/original_image218275ac-b039-473c-8bae-c876cb388d
 b1.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join The Ordinary for its first-ever experiential pop-up in it
 s hometown\, Toronto: The Markup Marché.\nThe Markup Marché pop-up will 
 highlight everyday essentials marketed and priced to reflect the exaggerat
 ed language and extreme markups often seen in the beauty world. For exampl
 e\, a banana is labelled as an All Natural Magical Energy-Boosting Bar pri
 ced at $175.90 or a High-Retention Cleansing Cylinder is in fact a $96.20 
 toilet roll. The Markup Marché will spark curiosity around beauty industr
 y marketing\, with each aisle\, shelf\, and product spotlighting facts and
  stats that unpack the very tactics seen across beauty today. Take a peek 
 behind the curtain of industry pricing and marketing tactics\, enjoy fresh
 ly squeezed juices from The Jargon Bar\, and receive a sample of The Ordin
 ary Hyaluronic Acid 2% + B5 (with Ceramides) at checkout.\nAt The Ordinary
 \, we prefer to speak in ordinary terms. Without added hype\, jargon or ma
 rketing fluff. Because the only words that really matter are the ingredien
 ts on the label. That’s why we name our clinical formulations after them
 . And charge a price that's accessible. Buy the ingredients\, not the hype
 .\nThe Markup Marché\nDATES & TIME:\nFriday\, May 8th: 11am - 7pm\nSaturd
 ay\, May 9th : 10am - 6pm\nLOCATION: 711 Queen Street West
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/the-ordinary-markup-marche-pop-up-toront
 o/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
