BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mother's Day at OpenTable
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260509T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260509T150000
UID:blogto-234275@blogto.com
DESCRIPTION:Mother’s Day is one of the biggest dining days of the year\,
  with dining  up 26 per cent in 2025\, year over year.¹ To help Torontoni
 ans plan a special meal for mom\, OpenTable has launched its annual Top 10
 0 Brunch and Lunch Restaurants for 2026 list\, ² featuring 26 restaurants
  in Toronto.\nNew consumer research shows nearly half (47%) of Torontonian
 s plan to dine out to celebrate Mother’s Day this year\, and 67% say din
 ing out is an important part of their Mother’s Day celebration. ³\n[Tor
 onto pitch only]: To make Mother’s Day extra special\, OpenTable is part
 nering with The Dorset\, one of the Top 100 Brunch and Lunch Restaurants f
 or 2026\, to offer a unique bookable experience.\nOn Saturday\, May 9\, th
 e day before Mother’s Day\, between 11am - 3pm\, The Dorset will host To
 ronto-based artist Ama Liyanage (Greyishteal) to create one-of-kind live w
 atercolour portraits. The experience is integrated into the restaurant’s
  Afternoon Tea offering\, giving diners and their moms or mother figures a
  personalized keepsake to take home from their celebration.\nThe painting 
 experience will come complimentary of OpenTable for those who have booked 
 afternoon tea.* Reservations can be made exclusively via OpenTable Experie
 nces. Limited spots are available.\n*OpenTable will cover the live paintin
 g experience only\; diners will still be responsible for the cost of their
  meal.\nA full list of the Toronto restaurants on this year’s list can b
 e found below:\nGrazie Toronto\, Toronto\nAllen's\, Toronto\nREIGN\, Toron
 to\nLe Sélect Bistro\, Toronto\nAbrielle\, Toronto\nThe Lunch Lady\, Toro
 nto\nAmal Restaurant\, Toronto\nAloette\, Toronto\nCafé Boulud\, Toronto\
 nQueens Harbour\, Toronto\nThe Berczy\, Toronto\nTerroni Price\, Toronto\n
 Miss Likklemores\, Toronto\nLOUIX LOUIS\, Toronto\nStock Bar\, Toronto\nEl
  Catrin\, Toronto\nThe Dorset\, Toronto\nDaphne\, Toronto\nAlder\, Toronto
 \nUnion\, Toronto\nChubby's Jamaican Kitchen\, Toronto\nRH Courtyard Resta
 urant at RH Toronto\, Toronto\nKŌST\, Toronto\nAuberge du Pommier\, Toron
 to\nPai Northern Thai - Uptown\, Toronto\nGeneral Public\, Toronto\nThe fu
 ll media release is included below with the Top 100 Brunch and Lunch Resta
 urants in Canada for 2026\, alongside this year’s Mother’s Day dining 
 trends. Laure Bornet\, Senior Vice President of International Growth at Op
 enTable\, is available to speak about the trends if of interest.\nBest\,\n
 xx\nNotes to Editors\nOpenTable Data: OpenTable looked at seated diners fr
 om online reservations from all active restaurants on the OpenTable platfo
 rm in Canada on May 11\, 2025 and compared it to the corresponding date pe
 riod in 2024 (May 12\, 2024)\, as well as analysing dining in 2025.\nThe T
 op 100 Brunch and Lunch Restaurants in Canada 2026 Methodology: OpenTable'
 s Top 100 Restaurants for Brunch and Lunch in Canada for 2026 list is gene
 rated from over 1 million from verified OpenTable diners and dining metric
 s from 1st March 2025 - 28th February 2026. Restaurants with a minimum thr
 eshold of diner reviews were considered and evaluated by a compilation of 
 unique data points\, including diner ratings\, the percentage of five star
  reviews\, the number of alerts set\, the percentage of reservations made 
 in advance\, percentage of capacity and direct searches. Metrics were weig
 hted to comprise an overall score. The qualified restaurants were then fil
 tered on having a minimum number of brunch reviews and Sunday lunch availa
 bility. The resulting list appears A-Z\, not in ranked order.\nConsumer Re
 search Methodology: An online survey was conducted by Ripple Research amon
 g 1500 CA consumers celebrating Mother’s Day\, including 637 who are bei
 ng celebrated as mothers/mother figures and will be celebrating other moth
 ers/mother figures\, and a quota of 200 for major cities. Fieldwork was co
 nducted between 16th March 2026 and 19th March 2026. All data was collecte
 d in accordance with MRS (Market Research Society) and ESOMAR guidelines\,
  ensuring ethical standards and robust data quality.
LOCATION:The Dorset
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/mothers-day-at-opentable-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mothers Day Baby Art Workshop in Toronto
