BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Play Mas: A Portrait of Carnival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260509T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260509T180000
UID:blogto-233790@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/17/original_image11e447e5-8eec-4a5c-b541-f0338b2ee9
 84.jpg
DESCRIPTION:For the 2026 Contact Photography Festival\, Gallery 1888 is pr
 oud to present the work of local photographer Wayne Salmon. For over twent
 y-five years\, Wayne Salmon has photographed Carnival not only as spectacl
 e\, but as a living cultural practice. Play Mas traces the connection betw
 een Trinidad’s Carnival and its continuation in Toronto\, focusing on th
 e people who build\, sustain\, and pass on these traditions across generat
 ions.\nThe images present Carnival as something lived and carried—shaped
  by histories of movement and diaspora\, from the Middle Passage to the pr
 esent. Through Salmon’s work\, Carnival emerges as an ongoing expression
  of identity\, community\, and continuity.
LOCATION:Gallery 1888
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/play-mas-a-portrait-of-carnival-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
