BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Queer Art Club: Draw A Drag Queen
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260509T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260509T160000
UID:blogto-233769@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/17/original_imagea295c08d-4fba-47fa-ba4e-505a4ff5bb
 9a.jpg
DESCRIPTION:In this edition of Queer Art Club we will be learning how to f
 igure draw with a drag performer!\nDate: Saturday May 9 (2-4PM)\nLocation:
  George Chuvalo Neighbourhood Centre\nTickets: Register on Eventbrite\, ti
 ckets are $25\nYou’ll learn the basics of costumed figure drawing in thi
 s beginner-friendly workshop. Together\, we’ll break down the seven type
 s of fabric folds and learning how to spot them on a clothed model and und
 erstand how the body’s form shapes the drapery. Connect with your commun
 ity\, build your skills\, and draw alongside a fabulous drag model: Seyonc
 e Knows!\nSketchbooks and pencils will be available for all participants. 
 Guests who wish to use additional materials are welcome to bring their own
  supplies\; however\, we kindly ask that these be limited to dry media or 
 a small watercolor set.\nIn this workshop with step-by-step guidance you w
 ill:\n- Sketch with pencil and paper (or bring your favourite materials!)\
 n- Learn the basics of drawing the figure and how fabric moves and flows\n
 - Try out quick\, simplified figure sketches using handy shorthand techniq
 ues\n- Spot tension points and discover the magic of the seven fabric fold
 s\n- Create a series of lively\, timed drawings of a drag performer\nEach 
 participant will leave with their sketchbooks and a solid knowledge of how
  fabric intetacts on the human figure!\nAccessibility: The workshop will b
 e on the second floor of George Chuvalo Neighbourhood Centre. The centre i
 s fully accessible. All entrances and restrooms are wheelchair accessible\
 , and there is an elevator available to access the second floor.\nSam Brai
 thwaite has been teaching figure drawing at Seneca Polytechnic for 5 years
  and working in the animation industry for 13. Sam has worked on TV shows 
 such as Blues Clues and You\, Wild Kratts\, and Angry Birds Summer Madness
 . For independents projects Sam has created music videos for Ria Mae and D
 .W Waterson.
LOCATION:George Chuvalo Neighbourhood Centre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/queer-art-club-draw-a-drag-queen-toronto
 /
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
