 ogress - but also honours moms from coast-to-coast.\nShow your support for
  breast cancer research by incorporating a walk into your daily activities
 . Walk with your colleagues on your lunch break\, organize a hike with fri
 ends on your favourite trail\, or rally your family for a special walk in 
 your neighbourhood on Mother's Day.\nThe more we know about breast cancer\
 , the sooner we can end it.\nDo you live in the GTA? Join our in-person wa
 lk in Mississauga!\nIn Person Event Details:\nDate: Sunday\, May 10\, 2026
 \nRegistration: 9:00am\n5KM Walk: 10:00am\nLocation: Streetsville Memorial
  Park (355 Church St. Mississauga\, ON)
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/breast-cancer-canada-mothers-day-walk-20
 26-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BRUNCH: Mother's Day Kitchen by Alissa Kondogiannis
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260510T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260510T143000
UID:blogto-234260@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/27/original_image917a3dec-0dc7-4703-92f9-783b45531d
 5b.jpg
DESCRIPTION:For many people\, the warm\, inviting smell of something delic
 ious baking in the oven is enough to transport them to their Mother's or G
 randmother's kitchen. This Mother's Day we celebrate moms with a beautiful
  buffet brunch of sophisticated\, warm-from-the-oven tarts\, colourful\, f
 resh salads\, and exquisite pastries prepared with love by Alissa Kondogia
 nnis. She has chosen a handful of her favourite brunch recipes for a gorge
 ous spread of elegant hand-made\, plant-forward dishes for sharing.\n----\
 nWelcome Cocktail\nHibiscus mimosa [regular or non-acloholic]\nRoasted Asp
 aragus\, Feta and Lemon Tart\nPuff pastry tart of fresh\, local Spring asp
 aragus\, creamy feta cheese and bright lemon zest with a seeded crust.\nCh
 eddar and Caramelized Onion Galette\nSharp cheddar and sweet\, caramelized
  onions wrapped in light\, handmade pastry.\nGruyère Butter Bean Crêpes\
 nButter beans in a Gruyère béchamel with a mild curry accent\, baked unt
 il golden and drizzled with chutney.\nSalmon Niçoise with a Twist\nSesame
 -crusted salmon\, pink\, beet-marinated eggs\, tomatoes\, green beans\, ba
 by potatoes with roasted olives and roasted radishes.\nSpinach\, Strawberr
 y and Chèvre Salad\nWith toasted pecans and balsamic vinaigrette.\nPillow
 y Cinnamon Buns\nslathered with cream cheese and orange zest frosting.\nMi
 ni Pistachio Loaves\nLuscious olive oil cake with ground almonds\, pistach
 ios and lemon zest\, delicately glazed and dusted with ground pistachios.\
 nFresh Fruit Salad\nColourful selection of fresh fruits and berries\nHomem
 ade Iced Teas\nFresh strawberry with orange pekoe\, and passion fruit & pe
 ach herbal iced tea.\nBottomless coffee and tea\n-----\nMother's Day Deals
 \nKids under 12 are 1/2 price • Infants under 2 yrs are free\nBook a tab
 le of 8 & Mom comes for free!\n(Buy 7\, Get 8 = 1 free ticket or $10 off e
 ach ticket)\n-----\nAlissa Kondogiannis runs a small catering company Nort
 h of the Toronto\, focusing on Shabbat dinners and Jewish comfort food. Sh
 e has taught babka and challah classes for years\, here at The Depanneur a
 s well as in her Thornhill Community. You can find her online at Barnstar 
 Kitchen. @barnstarkitchen
LOCATION:The Depanneur
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/brunch-mothers-day-kitchen-by-alissa-kon
 dogiannis-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
