BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TFS Presents a Mother's Day Musical Double Feature
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260510T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260510T170000
UID:blogto-233610@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/14/original_image93b4fdac-961f-416f-8bcb-2306c2a9cd
 76.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Make it a Mother’s Day outing at the movies with a musical d
 ouble feature that’s equal parts sparkle and heart. Start with Gold Digg
 ers of 1933\, the ultimate backstage crowd-pleaser\, featuring the famous 
 Busby Berkeley production numbers that basically invented “movie musical
  spectacle.” Then settle into Lili\, a tender\, charming story set aroun
 d a travelling carnival - a film that’s pure classic-Hollywood warmth. T
 his is the film that introduced the hit song Hi-Lili\, Hi-Lo! Two timeless
  films\, one great afternoon\, and a perfect excuse to go to the theatre!
LOCATION:Paradise Theatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/tfs-presents-a-mothers-day-musical-doubl
 e-feature-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:We\, Otherwise - Music& Art Residency at Tranzac
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260510T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260510T213000
UID:blogto-232165@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/03/13/original_image32bf8dea-0318-4c85-84d8-3ad3cac881
 93.jpg
DESCRIPTION:What happens when music becomes a place to meet?\nWe are a col
 lective of three culturally diverse women working across music\, curation\
 , and arts administration\, brought together by a shared interest in creat
 ing spaces where artists and audiences can encounter one another more deep
 ly.\nThis project proposes a recurring\, intimate Sunday series designed a
 s a cultural meeting point. Each month\, we invite two artists from differ
 ent cultural backgrounds to share an evening where performance\, dialogue\
 , and gathering are intentionally woven together.\nThe evening unfolds in 
 three parts:\n-  a conversation where the invited musicians speak about th
 eir practice\, lineage\, and influences\;\n-  a live musical exchange wher
 e they respond to one another in real time\;\n-  a participatory artistic 
 activation that invites the audience to move from observers to co-holders 
 of the space.\nOur intention is to create nights that feel thoughtful\, al
 ive\, and relational\, where artists are not only presented\, but genuinel
 y hosted\, and where cultural difference becomes a place for curiosity\, l
 istening\, and connection.
LOCATION:Tranzac Club
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/we-otherwise-music-art-residency-at-tran
 zac-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:WE REALLY LIKE HER! presents FUNNY GIRL
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260510T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260510T183000
UID:blogto-234139@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/24/original_imagecd83c097-e7da-4797-bef4-8130e0cf59
 43.jpg
DESCRIPTION:This Mother’s Day\, We Really Like Her! invites you to put o
 n your fave leopard coat and join them for a matinee of FUNNY GIRL (1968).
 \nBased on the hit Broadway show also penned by Isobel Lennart (Love Me or
  Leave Me\, The Sundowners)\, this beloved movie musical firmly establishe
 d Barbra Streisand as one of our greatest stars. It’s also probably one 
 of your mom’s favourite movies\, or\, at the very least\, reminds you of
  one of the amazing women in your life.\nPresenting a fictionalized versio
 n of comedian Fanny Brice’s career and tumultuous relationship with gamb
 ler Nick Arnstein (played by a swoon-worthy Omar Sharif)\, Funny Girl is\,
  much like Babs\, a winning blend of comedy and melodrama. And it’s not 
 just her timeless performance that will sweep you off your feet. Paired wi
 th Lennart’s sharp script\, the lush production design\, period costumin
 g by Irene Sharaff (West Side Story\, A Star is Born)\, and standout songs
  like “Don’t Rain on My Parade” (duh) and “My Man” (sob) make th
 e film’s nearly three-hour runtime fly by faster than Fanny on skates.\n
 Simply gorgeous from every angle\, Funny Girl is a film that demands to be
  seen on the big screen. Preferably with an adoring crowd of people who ne
 ed people.
LOCATION:Revue Cinema
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/we-really-like-her-presents-funny-girl-t
 oronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
