BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beer 101: From Grain to Glass by Joke Van Loon
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260515T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260515T210000
UID:blogto-234261@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/27/original_image0945815b-6005-41d6-b2ff-f0edf1693d
 1d.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Beer can seem simple at first glance: it’s a combination of 
 grain\, hops\, yeast and water. Yet small changes in ingredients and brewi
 ng techniques can create an incredible range of flavours\, from crisp and 
 refreshing to rich\, fruity\, sour or bitter.\nIn this interactive masterc
 lass\, zythologist (beer connoisseur) Joke Van Loon (Tasting Talks) takes 
 you on a journey from the origins of brewing to the fundamentals of how be
 er is made—and how to enjoy it with confidence.\nWe’ll begin with a sh
 ort look at the history of beer and how brewing evolved from accidental fe
 rmentation to a refined craft. From there\, we’ll follow the brewing pro
 cess step by step\, using it as a guide to understand how each ingredient 
 influences what ends up in your glass.\nThrough a curated tasting flight\,
  we’ll explore:\nHow malt affects colour\, sweetness\, and body\nHow hop
 s contribute bitterness and aroma\nHow yeast and fermentation create flavo
 urs ranging from clean and crisp to fruity\, spicy\, or sour\nAlong the wa
 y\, you’ll taste a range of beer styles—from light and approachable to
  bold and expressive—each chosen to highlight a specific part of the bre
 wing process. Styles will include\, but not be limited to\, Vienna Lager\,
  Stout\, IPA\, Tripel and Sour.\nSimple food pairings will accompany the b
 eers to demonstrate how flavours interact and enhance one another.\nThis c
 lass is designed for both beginners and curious drinkers alike. No prior k
 nowledge needed—just an interest in discovering how beer really works an
 d how to enjoy it more fully.\n----\nJoke Van Loon is a Belgian beer enthu
 siast with a degree in clinical psychology who had a practice in Antwerp f
 or a decade. Her passion for all things brewing led her to becoming a cert
 ified Zythologist (aka beer sommelier) at the PIVA culinary school in Antw
 erp.\nShe moved to Toronto in 2025 and devoted herself fully to her studie
 s in beer\, creating Tasting Talks - a project that melds her fascination 
 with the topic with her love for connecting people. Making beer culture fu
 n\, approachable and engaging\, Joke aims to inspire creative tasting and 
 exploring outside of one's comfort zone. @tasting_talks\n'The world of bee
 r is so much bigger than most people imagine\, and I love creating welcomi
 ng spaces where they can learn\, explore\, discover new flavours\, and con
 nect with others over great beer.'
LOCATION:The Depanneur
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/beer-101-from-grain-to-glass-by-joke-van
 -loon-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
