DESCRIPTION:May 16\n8pm\n$15-$20 adv\n$25 doors\nJoin us for Frequency —
  a monthly live music series at Worth Gallery. Frequency spotlights BIPOC 
 musicians of varying genres through intimate\, stripped-back shows. Celebr
 ating sound\, connection\, and creative expression in Toronto's vibrant mu
 sic scene. Find your new favorite musician in your new favorite gallery.\n
 This edition of Frequency features Latavia\, a powerhouse vocalist who off
 ers healing through lyrics and melody.\nLatavia is an R&B/Soul singer-song
 writer from Brampton\, Ontario. Growing up in her grandfather's church\, s
 he began singing at the age of four and writing lyrics at age nine. Drawin
 g inspiration from '90s and early 2000's R&B\, she is influenced by iconic
  vocalists such as Whitney Houston\, Brandy and Jazmine Sullivan\, artists
  known for their emotional vulnerability\, powerful vocals and raw storyte
 lling. She creates emotionally honest music about self-worth\, love\, hear
 tbreak\, and personal growth. Through her artistry\, Latavia aims to inspi
 re healing\, reflection and empowerment. She has new music set to be relea
 sed this year.\nLocated in the lower gallery — down a flight of stairs.\
 nFor any other accessibility questions\, please feel free to reach out to 
 us.
