BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SING! The Toronto International Vocal Arts Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260519T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260519T233000
UID:blogto-233972@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/21/original_image3f66290b-4735-4bdb-8974-c571f13f81
 bc.jpg
DESCRIPTION:SING! The Toronto International Vocal Arts Festival is Canada
 ’s premier a cappella festival (singing without instruments). Held every
  year in May\, SING! presents a week of outstanding concerts featuring the
  human voice. We bring together thousands of professional singers (Canadia
 n and international)\, students\, teachers\, divas and in-the-shower belte
 rs.\nEVENTS:\n1. SING! in the Clubs: Art Battle\nLocation:  The Great Hall
 \nDate: Tuesday\, May 19 2026 at 7:30pm\nSING! and Art Battle collaborate 
 once again to bring you a night of Beatboxing and live competitive paintin
 g. Featuring Canadian Beatbox Champion Scott Jackson (Canada’s Got Talen
 t Finalist\, NBA halftime shows). Join us for an epic art showdown\, the l
 ast one of the year in Toronto! Creativity knows no bounds! Watch as maste
 rful artists craft stunning masterpieces in just 20 minutes per round. Be 
 part of the decision-making process and vote for the ultimate champion. An
 d don't miss your chance to own a piece of the action with the silent auct
 ion of all original works!\nTICKETS: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/art-batt
 le-toronto-may-19-2026-tickets-1986959895535?aff=ebdsoporgprofile\n2. SING
 ! Free: Preview event\nLocation: Nathan Phillips Square\nDate: Wednesday\,
  May 20\, 2026\, from 5:30pm to 7:30pm\nOur annual free outdoor concert in
  the heart of Toronto\, featuring a variety of vocal groups and styles. Th
 is year will feature FreePlay\, City Choir\, Peterborough Pop Ensemble\, a
 nd more!\n3. SING! Free: Outdoor Concerts\nLocation: College Park\nDate: T
 hursday May 21\, 2026 from 5:00 to 7:00pm\nFor the first time ever\, SING!
  brings free outdoor concerts to College Park at Yonge and College\, featu
 ring 2 hours of eclectic vocal music.\n4. SING! in Concert: Countermeasure
  - One More Spin\nLocation: Paradise Theatre\nDate: Friday\, May 22\, Door
 s 7pm\, Show 7:30pm\nAfter sixteen years of globetrotting\, collaborating\
 , recording\, and general merrymaking\, Countermeasure announces their fin
 al concert. Join the group for a landmark celebration of music\, memories\
 , and friendship - drawing from audience favourites and deep cuts.\nTICKET
 S: https://singtoronto.tickit.ca/events/34562\n5. SING! Music Business Sum
 mit: Industry Roundtable Discussions\nDate: Saturday\, May 23 - TELUS Cent
 re for Performance and Learning\nThis is a unique opportunity to connect c
 losely with experts from many aspects of the music industry. Attendees wil
 l sign up for 15-minute slots to discuss their own questions and ideas. Me
 etings take place with a small group seated around a table and are on a fi
 rst-come\, first-served basis\, so come early to sign up for the people yo
 u want to meet. Building a career in music? You need to be here. An experi
 enced professional? This is great networking for you. Decades of experienc
 e shared in one session!\nTICKETS: https://singtoronto.tickit.ca/events/34
 568\n6. SING! and Learn: Songwriting\nDATE: Saturday May 23 at 4pm - Royal
  Conservatory of Music\nIn this workshop\, Aaron Jensen—musical director
 /composer for Schitt’s Creek and collaborator with Grammy and JUNO award
 -winning artists—shares his creative process and gives you step-by-step 
 advice on writing your own songs. It is perfect for anyone getting ready t
 o dive in\, or practicing songwriters looking for more inspiration and too
 ls.\nTICKETS: https://singtoronto.tickit.ca/events/33086\n7. SING! Canadia
 n A Cappella Championships\nLOCATION: Koerner Hall at the TELUS Centre for
  Performance & Learning\nDATE: Saturday\, May 23 at 7pm\nFollowing up on t
 he overwhelming success of last year’s inaugural competition\, we are th
 rilled to make this year even bigger and better! This year's competition w
 ill feature 16 groups battling it out across four categories: High School\
 , Collegiate/University\, Open\, and the new Barbershop division.\nTICKETS
 : https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/438601\n8. Aca-Singalong with Pitc
 h Perfect's Music Director Deke Sharon and special guests Splüsh\nLOCATIO
 N: Royal Ontario Museum\nDATE: Sunday May 24\, 1:00pm\nJoin the legendary 
 Deke Sharon\, 'Father of Contemporary A Cappella'\, to learn and sing a so
 ng from the famous movie franchise.\nTICKETS: https://singtoronto.tickit.c
 a/events/31698\n9. SING! Pass the Mic Night\nLOCATION: Royal Ontario Museu
 m\nDATE: Sunday\, May 24\, 7:00pm\nThis event invites all 2026 Championshi
 p applicants and finalists\, along with their friends and family\, to gath
 er at the Royal Ontario Museum’s Signy & Cléophée Eaton Theatre for a 
 relaxed\, non-competitive evening of music. Ensembles take turns “passin
 g the mic” to share a song\, celebrating community\, connection\, and th
 e joy of a cappella.\nTICKETS: https://singtoronto.tickit.ca/events/31727\
 n10. Great North Beatbox Festival\nLOCATION: The Rec Room\nBeatbox Canada 
 and SING! present the Great North Beatbox Festival\, the largest celebrati
 on of beatboxing in North America! Bringing together the Canadian Beatbox 
 Championships\, Great North Battle and All from the Mouth Showcase competi
 tion for the first time in one weekend.\nDay 1 | Friday May 29th - All Fro
 m the Mouth Showcase\nDay 2 | Saturday May 30th - Canadian Beatbox Champio
 nships\nDay 3 | Sunday May 31st - Great North Battle\n11. SING! and Learn:
  The Real Group presents Sing with Confidence\nLOCATION: Royal Ontario Mus
 eum\nDATE: Monday\, June 1\, at 4pm\nStep into your voice with confidence 
 in this fun and welcoming workshop led by members of Swedish vocal legends
  The Real Group. Open to all ages and experience levels\, this session is 
 designed for all levels of singers looking to strengthen their presence an
 d trust in their own sound.\nTICKETS: https://singtoronto.tickit.ca/events
 /34782\n12. SING! In Concert: SING! with Pride\nLOCATION: Royal Ontario Mu
 seum\nDATE: Monday June 1\, 7:30pm\nExperience the world-class vocal artis
 try of The Real Group\, the legendary Swedish quintet that redefined a cap
 pella. Blending jazz\, pop\, and Nordic choral music\, they create a "voic
 e-only" sound so rich you’ll forget there are no instruments on stage.\n
 Presented as an official Pride Toronto Major Cultural event\, this perform
 ance celebrates the power of harmony\, community\, and creative expression
 . Also featuring opening group Singing Out Choir\, and a special presentat
 ion of the SING! Toronto Legacy Award to Heather Bambrick.\nTICKETS: https
 ://singtoronto.tickit.ca/events/32858\nSOME EVENT TIMES ARE UNKNOWN SO A R
 OUGH ESTIMATE IS IN THE EVENT SECTION BELOW
LOCATION:Multiple Venues
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/sing-the-toronto-international-vocal-art
 s-festival-toronto-4/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
