END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Martini Madness
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260521T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260521T230000
UID:blogto-233392@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/09/original_imageb74450c7-dbb7-4d53-8690-3fcbba5654
 81.jpg
DESCRIPTION:One of Toronto’s favourite fundraising events is back! Marti
 ni Madness returns this May 2026\, presented by CIBC and The Andlauer Fami
 ly. The event brings together cocktail enthusiasts\, community leaders\, a
 nd supporters for an unforgettable evening in support of life-changing med
 ical research.\nIn support of the GEM Project through the Sinai Health Fou
 ndation\, Martini Madness raises critical funds to help uncover the causes
  of Crohn’s disease and ulcerative colitis—two chronic conditions affe
 cting more than 320\,000 Canadians.\nThe Toronto event will feature an ele
 vated\, all-inclusive experience\, where guests can enjoy unlimited signat
 ure martinis crafted by top mixologists\, curated food stations\, and a li
 vely atmosphere designed for connection and celebration. A premium raffle 
 will also offer exclusive items and experiences\, with all proceeds suppor
 ting research efforts that are changing lives.\nWith thousands of Canadian
 s diagnosed with inflammatory bowel disease each year—including massivel
 y increasing rates in children and young adults—the need for continued r
 esearch and innovation has never been more urgent.
LOCATION:Ricarda's
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/martini-madness-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Music TORONTO - Penderecki String Quartet
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260521T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260521T210000
UID:blogto-221807@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2025/07/27/original_imageb0f995ac-20ee-4b32-8f0f-0a711ba51c
 94.jpg
DESCRIPTION:The Penderecki String Quartet began their journey in Poland\, 
 winning the prestigious Penderecki Prize at the 1986 National Chamber Musi
 c Competition in Łódź. Since 1991\, they have been Quartet-in-Residence
  at Wilfrid Laurier University\, shaping one of Canada’s leading string 
 programs. Renowned for their commitment to contemporary music\, the Pender
 ecki Quartet has commissioned and performed over 100 new works. This seaso
 n\, they present a world premiere collaboration with rapper Shad and compo
 ser Nicole Lizée\, featuring the suite Something Good Is Gonna Happen…I
  Don’t Know When… Closing the program\, Roman Borys—cellist of the G
 ryphon Trio and Artistic Director of Music TORONTO—joins the quartet to 
 perform Schubert’s sublime Quintet in C Major. Experience an inspiring e
 vening of innovative new music alongside timeless classical masterpieces.\
 nTickets: $60-$65\n416-366-7723
LOCATION:Jane Mallett Theatre\, St. Lawrence Centre for the Arts
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/music-toronto-penderecki-string-quartet-
 toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:North Indian Flatbreads by Ekta Maheshwari
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260521T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260521T210000
UID:blogto-234289@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/28/original_image9a3c3310-c794-4d53-b72f-7618bfe3bf
 07.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Master the techniques behind some popular traditional Indian f
 lat-breads in this fun\, hands-on class with baker\, chef and teacher Ekta
  Maheshwari. Together you’ll cook some beloved everyday traditional brea
 ds along with a lesser-known regional stuffed breads from Bikaner in Rajas
 than province in India's Northwest.\nBeetroot Parathas — A playful twist
  on plain parathas\, folded and rolled into their signature triangular sha
 pe.\nAloo Parathas — Soft\, hearty flatbreads filled with spiced mashed 
 potatoes — a global favorite for good reason.\nBesan Parathas  — A Raj
 asthani stuffed flatbread with a savory gram-flour filling\; a long-standi
 ng family favourite of Ekta’s that is always prepared in big batches for
  long travels as it tastes even better the next day!\nHome-style Chole / C
 hana Masala — a simple\, comforting chickpea curry perfect for everyday 
 meals\nMint & Cucumber Raita — yogurt-based side dish that is cooling an
 d aids digestion\nThe class begins with kneading two types of doughs\; the
  classic dough for stuffed parathas\, and another\, colourful version for 
 beetroot parathas. As you work with different hydrations and inclusions\, 
 you will be guided to develop an understanding of how traditional flatbrea
 d doughs come together.\nWhile the doughs rest\, participants will work in
  groups and prepare the side dishes along with the fillings for both the s
 tuffed parathas. You’ll also learn to make a quick\, home-style chole / 
 chana masala\, a warm chickpea curry that's the perfect pairing for fresh\
 , plain parathas\, or with stuffed parathas for a more indulgent experienc
 e.\nAfter learning how to shape\, roll and griddle your own flatbreads\, p
 articipants will sit down to enjoy some of their handiwork\, along with a 
 cool\, fresh yogurt raita\, and a little mango or chili pickle to complete
  the meal. Any extra breads in the class can be taken home — feel free t
 o bring containers!\nLight refreshments will be provided to enjoy before b
 eginning the class\, and you can bring your own rolling pin to the class. 
 There will also be the opportunity to purchase some of the chef's homemade
  slow-roasted spice blends & North Indian seasonings.\nCome curious\, come
  hungry!\n-----\nEkta Maheshwari is a Chef Instructor at George Brown Coll
 ege\, where she shares her passion for bread baking. She is also the Owner
  and Chef at Arth Toronto\, a farmers’ market based business\, where she
  celebrates slow-cooked\, from-scratch dishes inspired by both - tradition
 al Indian home cooking and Ontario’s vibrant seasonal produce. Her teach
 ing style blends deep culinary knowledge with warmth\, curiosity and a lov
 e for sharing food traditions. @arth.toronto
LOCATION:The Depanneur
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/north-indian-flatbreads-by-ekta-maheshwa
 ri-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
