BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Her Sports Fest
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260522T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260523T160000
UID:blogto-234312@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/28/original_imagefcfe106a-ff4b-46c2-8c35-755f6ba51d
 0c.jpg
DESCRIPTION:A new\, hands-on celebration of girls and women in sport is co
 ming to Toronto this spring. The inaugural Her Sports Fest will take place
  May 22–24\, 2026 at The Hangar Sport and Events Centre in Downsview Par
 k\, bringing together girls and women of all ages for a dynamic\, action-p
 acked weekend designed to get more girls and women active in sport.\nBuilt
  around four core themes — “Try It. Learn It. Find It. Amp It.” — 
 Her Sports Fest offers an inclusive\, interactive space where participants
  can discover new sports\, build skills\, connect with others\, and celebr
 ate their journey in sport. On-site activations and live demonstrations wi
 ll feature a range of sports — including biathlon\, flag football\, socc
 er\, golf\, skateboarding\, athletics\, sailing and many more.\nWeekend Pr
 ogramming Highlights\nFriday\, May 22 – StrongHER Night Out (19+)\nThe w
 eekend kicks off with a high-energy\, adults-only experience from 6:30 pm 
 to 10:30 pm ET. StrongHER Night Out invites women to try new sports\, conn
 ect with the community\, and celebrate movement in a fun\, social setting.
  The first 200 attendees will receive a Her Sports Fest gift.\nSaturday\, 
 May 23 & Sunday\, May 24 – Youth Festival (Ages 8–18)\nProgramming run
 s from 10:00 am to 4:00 pm ET each day\, designed primarily for girls aged
  8 to 18\, with families\, friends\, and teammates welcome to join. Partic
 ipants will have the opportunity to explore multiple sports in a supportiv
 e\, confidence-building environment.
LOCATION:The Hangar Sport and Events Centre in Downsview Park
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/her-sports-fest-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
