BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Urban Garden Day Retreats
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260522T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260522T160000
UID:blogto-234405@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/29/original_imageed3874a3-0a7b-429a-91b2-a8173d12d9
 da.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Our Urban Garden Day Retreats are the perfect way to refresh w
 ithout leaving the city.\nIf you’re seeking rest\, healing\, and connect
 ion\, near to home and in a simple one-day format\, this retreat among the
  old growth trees in our English-style garden in the Beaches is for you.  
 Be Still Yoga Urban Garden Day Retreats provide:\nBeautiful Setting: Held 
 in our serene\, private English garden and home.\nRest & Reflection Time: 
 The day unfolds in an easy\, relaxing way\, with the emphasis on connectio
 n and relaxation.  Away from the yoga mats\, there are comfy chairs\, shad
 e\, and even a hammock.  And there’s always good food and fresh coffee o
 n hand.\nOn-site Chef: The fabulous Chef Mark will welcome you into the tr
 anquil space and provide fresh\, homemade and healthy drinks\, meals and s
 nacks.\nJapanese Soaker Tub:  Unwind by enjoying a dip in the BC Red Cedar
  oval tub.\nWhat happens on the day:\n9:30am: Doors Open.  Coffee\, light 
 breakfast and a chance to get to know the other guests in an informal\, re
 laxed setting.\n10:15 – 10:45am: Opening Circle and Satsang.  Begin the 
 day in a supportive\, facilitated sharing space where you will have the op
 portunity to forge deep\, meaningful connections.\n11 am – 12pm: Yin Yog
 a Session with Kathryn.  Mats\, blocks\, straps\, bolsters\, blankets\, an
 d eye pillows are all provided.\n12 – 1pm: Lunch/Free time.  Enjoy Chef 
 Mark’s delicious\, healthy\, fresh food.  Share time with new or old fri
 ends in the garden\, on the balcony\, or under the shade of the old oak tr
 ee.\n1 – 1:45pm: Garden Sound Bath and Nature Experience: Sensory-guided
  nature experience. Live sound journey accompaniment to Kathryn’s sessio
 ns including gongs\, percussion\, chimes and crystal bowls.\n1:45 – 2:30
 pm: Free Time.  Built-in spaciousness for optional journaling\, reflection
  and intentional rest.  Healthy snacks from Mark the Chef.\n2:30 – 3:15p
 m Yoga Nidra Session with Kathryn.  Calming extended meditation\, lying do
 wn in comfort and listening only.\n3:30 – 4pm: Closing Circle.  An oppor
 tunity to solidify new friendships\, reflect on the day\, and optionally s
 hare learnings together.\nOptional:\nPrivate Massage Therapy: Option to bo
 ok in with our in-house registered RMT.\nPrivate Chiropractic Therapy:  Op
 tion to book in with our in-house chiropractor.
LOCATION:Be Still Yoga Garden
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/urban-garden-day-retreats-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Where Dark Things Dwell - Opening May 22
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260522T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260522T210000
UID:blogto-234377@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/29/original_image0e3f36bb-a2e5-47fc-b42d-404fedf036
 c0.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Discover the sleepy village of Black Creek\, where in the nigh
 t: a strange curse will thrust you into the heart of a grim tale! Secret C
 ity Adventures is excited to re-partner with The Village at Black Creek to
  co-produce an immersive escape game adventure within the historic village
  itself.\nOn Friday\, May 22nd\, the bell will toll once again as Toronto
 ’s largest outdoor escape game returns. Beware the bell\, stranger. This
  unique and chilling experience will take you and yours on a dark and eeri
 e quest in order to lift a curse that befalls The Village at Black Creek\,
  but if the final bell tolls before the end of your journey\, then all sha
 ll be lost. Where Dark Things Dwell first launched in 2017 with sold-out r
 uns and rave reviews. Secret City Adventures is thrilled to bring back the
  mystery once again.\nWithin the buildings and pathways of Black Creek’s
  historical village\, teammates will use their wit and lamplight to solve 
 the old hamlets' thrilling puzzles. Where Dark Things Dwell blends immersi
 ve theatre\, escape room puzzles\, and team bonding into an unforgettable 
 experience. The location\, actors\, and blood-pumping narrative complete t
 he immersive atmosphere as teams work to lift the curse or be doomed to fa
 ll under its spell.\nWhere Dark Things Dwell is played in teams of 4 with 
 15 teams competing to save the village. The games run Friday and Saturday 
 nights at 6 pm and 9 pm until August 29 at 1000 Murray Ross Parkway. All g
 ames take place outdoors\, without the aid of technology\, in the open-air
  museum of The Village at Black Creek.\nSecret City Adventures is a place-
 based design studio bringing games to life through captivating storytellin
 g experiences. Secret City Adventures has pioneered these immersive escape
  game experiences within Ontario since 2014. Their games have animated som
 e of Toronto’s most notable landmarks: Casa Loma\, George Brown House\, 
 Chinatown\, and Toronto’s waterfront.\nThe Village at Black Creek hosts 
 40 historic buildings\, 70 rare and heritage breed animals\, 10 gardens gr
 owing flowers and plants from heirloom seeds\, and exciting programs that 
 engage people of all ages. Immerse yourself in the 1860s and explore an au
 thentically recreated country village of the Toronto region.
LOCATION:The Village at Black Creek
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/where-dark-things-dwell-opening-may-22-t
 oronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
