 gto.com/events/2026/04/21/original_image9a6810d8-ba74-4438-85e0-ef9f1c0ad9
 92.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Tafelmusik’s 2025/26 season finale at Koerner Hall salutes t
 his uplifting spirit with music by Ludwig van Beethoven and Joseph Bologne
 \, composers who embraced change and challenged the status quo.\nA trailbl
 azer in his own right\, the renowned Japanese-American violinist Shunske S
 ato makes his Tafelmusik debut directing these performances. Concertmaster
  of Concerto Köln and former Artistic Leader of the Netherlands Bach Soci
 ety\, Sato is known for performances that push the envelope and “dig dee
 per into his instrument” (Gramophone).\nLeading the orchestra from the v
 iolin\, Sato directs Beethoven’s Symphony no. 3\, “Eroica\,” a work 
 that profoundly changed the symphonic form while staying true to the compo
 ser’s ethos. Don’t miss your chance to experience Tafelmusik’s 2025/
 26 season finale at Koerner Hall May 29-31\, 2026. Buy tickets at tafelmus
 ik.org
LOCATION:Koerner Hall
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/beethoven-eroica-bologne-the-winds-of-ch
 ange-toronto/
