ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/21/original_image494c7d59-b876-4a8c-93aa-a37aa212d9
 df.jpg
DESCRIPTION:In partnership with the University of Toronto Faculty of Music
 .\nJoin us in the vibrant setting of STACKT Market\, where we bring togeth
 er leading voices in contemporary music\, cultural studies\, and performan
 ce to explore a provocative question: What would the musical canon look li
 ke if it began today?\nThrough a lively discussion\, we will examine how c
 ultural biases\, systemic exclusion\, and evolving values have shaped our 
 understanding of musical excellence\, and how a new canon might better ref
 lect the diversity and creativity of today’s global soundscape. Together
 \, we will reimagine legacy\, influence\, and innovation from a 21st-centu
 ry perspective.\nCome for the conversation\, then stay to enjoy the surrou
 nding food trucks and breweries with fellow audience members.\nFeaturing:\
 nAiyun Huang —Chair\nJason Young\nRena Roussin\nCharlie Wall-Andrews\nRa
 shaan Allwood
LOCATION:The Studio at STACKT Market
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/future-resonance-festival-the-new-canon-
 toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
