BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NYC jazz pianist\, world-touring Western Canadian vocalist to debu
 t at Jazz Bistro
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260531T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260531T203000
UID:blogto-234356@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/29/original_image4b21e0b8-17b5-4b16-8c55-b7120b777e
 5a.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Gershwin\, Porter\, ’n Me\nJoin us at the Jazz Bistro on Sun
 day May 31st  for vocal jazz from Vancouver and New York alongside our spe
 cialty crafted cocktails and delicious bistro fare.\nWestern Canadian Musi
 c Awards ‘Jazz Artist of the Year’ nominee Angela Verbrugge brings Ger
 shwin- and Cole Porter-era standards to life with her signature charm. A f
 inalist in the International Songwriting Competition\, Verbrugge weaves in
  timeless stories of the heart with her own Canadian jazz compositions and
  lyrics.\nMaking her Jazz Bistro debut\, the Vancouver Island-based artist
  is described as “both hip and a hoot” (JazzWeekly)\, and has toured i
 n Japan\, Hong Kong\, S. Korea\, Taiwan\, Türkiye\, the UK\, Germany\, Lu
 xembourg\, France\, Italy\, and coast to coast in Canada — all since 202
 1! She has released four albums to great reviews from the international ja
 zz press\, topped polls in JazzTimes and All About Jazz\, and is regularly
  played on leading jazz radio programs. Her recorded songs have been strea
 med almost a million times across platforms.\nBacked by a stellar piano tr
 io — Grammy-nominated NYC pianist Ray Gallon\, Jon Maharaj (bass)\, and 
 Morgan Childs (drums)—Jazz Bistro guests can expect a warm\, witty\, and
  uplifting performance featuring beloved classics and new favourites deliv
 ered with irresistible musical chemistry. Seating is limited. Book your ta
 ble now for an unforgettable evening of jazz standards\, original Canadian
  lyrics\, and heartfelt music.\n(416) 363-5299 to reserve\nOnly $20 cover\
 n“No maybes\; for Verbrugge\, now is definitely the time\,” – JazzTi
 mes Magazine\n“Listen and be delighted. Her art is her own\, and she off
 ers rare pleasures.” — JazzLives\n“As a lyricist Miss Verbrugge seem
 s to have “learned” from the best: one senses the wit of Dave Frishber
 g\, the glorious storytelling of Dorothy Fields and Johnny Mercer\, and 
 – all of that and a tinge of pathos that was the hallmark of songs by Co
 le Porter. However\, make no mistake\, these lyrics are singularly Miss Ve
 rbrugge’s. ”— That Canadian Magazine\, Raul da Gama\n“Pianist Ray 
 Gallon may be one of New York City’s best kept secrets. A veteran sidema
 n with a career spanning over four decades\, Gallon was mentored by greats
  including John Lewis\, and Jaki Byard.” – The New York Jazz Record\n
 “Ray Gallon possesses a unique rhythmic imagination and a wrought iron v
 ocabulary.” – Bill Charlap\nAngela Verbrugge (vocals)\nVancouver Islan
 d vocalist Angela Verbrugge was nominated for Jazz Artist of the Year at t
 he 2024 Western Canadian Music Awards. In 2025\, All About Jazz announced 
 that Verbrugge had topped their Reader Poll for Jazz Vocalist and in 2020 
 Angela won the JazzTimes’ Readers’ Poll for Best Female Vocalist. She 
 “possesses a winsome\, brightly-burnished\, pliable voice\, ample emotio
 nal intelligence\, and conspicuously good taste. Angela’s four albums fe
 ature standout arrangements of standards and original songs in the style o
 f the Great American Songbook. The projects received praise in All About J
 azz\, JazzTimes\, Jazzwise\, Couleurs France\, Syncopated Times\, Jersey J
 azz\, LA Jazz Scene and publications around the world leading to tours to 
 Japan\, Taiwan\, Hong Kong\, China\, S. Korea\, Türkiye\, the UK\, German
 y\, France\, Luxembourg and eight provinces — all since 2021. Her music 
 has charted on JazzWeek\, been featured by CBC and NPR\, and she held the 
 number one spot on the Earshot Jazz charts for multiple weeks. Angela’s 
 tracks have been streamed a million times across streaming platforms since
  her debut in 2019.\nRay Gallon (piano)\nTo listen to pianist Ray Gallon i
 s to take a journey through the great lineage of jazz piano from its incep
 tion all the way up to the cutting-edge present. His playing is imbued wit
 h the vocabulary\, sensibilities and soul of the very architects of the ja
 zz artform. Born\, raised and living his whole life in Manhattan\, NYC pia
 nist Ray Gallon has been a mainstay on the jazz scene for over thirty-five
  years. Rooted in bebop and blues\, his expressive\, swingin’ playing me
 lds old and new into a fresh\, original style. As a young player\, Ray was
  taken under the wing of piano giants John Lewis\, Hank Jones\, and Jaki B
 yard. He has performed at major jazz festivals and venues around the world
  with such luminaries as Ron Carter\, Lionel Hampton\, Art Farmer\, Benny 
 Golson\, George Adams\, Les Paul\, and Wycliffe Gordon. Ray has appeared a
 t the White House and the Kennedy Center\, sharing the stage with jazz leg
 ends including Dizzy Gillespie\, Milt Jackson\, Sweets Edison\, and Joe Wi
 lliams. An in-demand accompanist\, he has worked with many vocal greats\, 
 including Jon Hendricks\, Sheila Jordan\, Dakota Staton\, Gloria Lynne\, J
 ane Monheit and Chaka Khan. Ray’s Cellar Live recordings include such lu
 minaries as Kenny Washington\, Ron Carter\, and Lewis Nash\, and Ahmad Jam
 al called his recorded work “extraordinary”.\nJon Maharaj (bass)\nJon 
 Maharaj is a JUNO-award winning bassist who has performed and / or recorde
 d with The Tenors\, Emilie-Claire Barlow\, Allison Au\, Amanda Tosoff and 
 many others. He has toured North America extensively with a variety of art
 ists and has performed overseas everywhere from Tokyo to Monte Carlo. Jon 
 was also the bassist in the Canadian company of the multiple award-winning
  musical Come From Away\, where he got to perform the show for over 1 mill
 ion people over the course of its record-breaking run.\nMorgan Childs (dru
 ms)\nBC-born Morgan Childs has established himself as a first-call drummer
  for many leading Canadian and international jazz artists. Morgan has four
  recordings to his name as a leader. Awards to his credit include three co
 nsecutive CBC Galaxie Rising Star Awards\, as well as the Grand Prix du Ja
 zz at the Montreal Jazz Festival. Other notable artists Morgan\nhas perfor
 med and recorded with include Zach Brock (Snarky Puppy)\, Phil Dwyer\, Kel
 ly Jefferson\, Bernie Senensky\, Eric Alexander\, Ingrid and Christine Jen
 sen\, Ian Hendrickson-Smith(The Roots)\, Kirk MacDonald\, and Pat Labarber
 a. Morgan has appeared on stages across Canada and around the world\, incl
 uding the US\, Mexico\, England\, Ukraine\, and India.
LOCATION:Jazz Bistro
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/nyc-jazz-pianist-world-touring-western-c
 anadian-vocalist-to-debut-at-jazz-bistro-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Plant-Based Moroccan Cooking by Salma Boudina
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260531T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260531T143000
UID:blogto-234322@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/28/original_image8617b8e1-ed33-490e-aa1f-1bbee02a41
 c4.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join Salma Boudina for a delicious introduction to the the vib
 rant world of vegetarian Moroccan cuisine. We begin with adas\, a beloved 
 Moroccan dish of lentils gently simmered with onion\, tomatoes\, and a fra
 grant blend of authentic spices\, a comforting staple found in homes acros
 s the country. You’ll also prepare tender carrots (khizzou) dressed with
  chermoula\, a spicy\, tangy and aromatic North African condiment of of he
 rbs\, garlic\, and spices that brings bold character to every bite.\nThen 
 there is chlada dyal btata\, a rustic potato salad with garlic and parsley
 \, and extra virgin olive oil — simple\, hearty\, and full of flavour. F
 reshness takes centre stage with chlada dyal lkhyar w maticha — an iconi
 c tomato and cucumber salad that one would find on every Moroccan table 
 — bright and juicy\, simply dressed to highlight the quality of each ing
 redient.\nTo finish\, we’ll prepare roz bal hlib\, a delicate non-dairy 
 rice pudding infused with orange blossom water\, offering a creamy texture
  and a beautifully floral aroma that lingers softly\, the perfect sweet en
 ding. Join us for a fun\, hands-on cooking experience where every dish ref
 lects the warmth and rich flavours of Moroccan tradition\nNote: This meal 
 is vegan\n-----\nSalma Boudina is passionate about preserving and sharing 
 the rich heritage of Moroccan cuisine. She has spent years collecting gran
 dmothers’ recipes and capturing the techniques and secrets behind tradit
 ional dishes\, knowledge that is often passed down orally from one generat
 ion to the next. With a background in Hospitality Management and a deep ap
 preciation for cultural traditions\, Salma approaches cooking as both a cr
 aft and a form of storytelling. Through her workshops\, Salma aims to make
  traditional Moroccan cooking accessible and approachable\, helping partic
 ipants build confidence in the kitchen while connecting to the history and
  meaning behind each dish.\n-----\nThe Depanneur is where Interesting Food
  Things happen. For more than a decade The Dep has been showcasing Toronto
 ’s remarkable culinary diversity by hosting unique food events. @thedepa
 nneur
LOCATION:The Depanneur
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/plant-based-moroccan-cooking-by-salma-bo
 udina-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rock & Roll Life Drawing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260531T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260531T160000
UID:blogto-234512@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/02/original_image43b99328-3276-4edb-b505-eb41b4492b
 4d.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Gwartzman’s and the El Mocambo are kicking off the summer wi
 th a rockin’ event for Toronto’s biggest mashup: Rock & Roll Life Draw
 ing! We’ll be joined by our three models\, Captain Mac\, Glinda Mercury\
 , and Katalina\, whose backgrounds span burlesque\, circus and traditional
  art modelling. They will be dressed in their rock and roll best with dyna
 mic poses\, so come prepared for an amazing self-guided costumed session. 
 Attendees are also encouraged to dress on-theme!\nPractice life drawing\, 
 capture the historic interior\, or find inspiration under the neon palms a
 nd create something abstract. This is your chance to draw the El Mocambo l
 ike you've never seen it.\nBring your pencils\, pens\, pastels\, paper\, a
 nd your other favourite dry media. To avoid mess\, we will not be permitti
 ng wet media\, paint\, ink\, or open containers of water. Forgot your sket
 chbook and sharpener? Stop over at Gwartzman’s – you’ll get a specia
 l 20% discount.\nThe Draw:\nWe’ve been neighbours for decades\, and we c
 an’t think of a better collaboration – joining the forces of Toronto
 ’s longest standing art supply store and most legendary music venue. Com
 e celebrate Toronto’s arts and music scene with Gwartzman’s and the El
  Mocambo!\nOur generous sponsors will be providing all attendees with an a
 mazing swag bag - including gifts from Leuchtturm1917\, Pentel\, Liquitex 
 and more! All ticket holders will be entered to win a huge raffle prize wi
 th items from Caran d’Ache\, etchr\, to name a few.\nWe’ve also curate
 d a special drawing scavenger hunt just for you\, shared the day of. To ma
 ximize the sketching fun\, try and find all the different sights we’ve s
 et for you throughout the event!
LOCATION:El Mocambo
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/rock-roll-life-drawing-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
