BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"Bucket Lister" 8-Day Annual Camping Road Trip
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T203000
UID:blogto-231433@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/02/26/original_image76bb8c2d-0f15-4f21-96dd-42ac5949bd
 00.jpg
DESCRIPTION:On June 12th\, this one-off annual tour turns Ontario into you
 r very own playground for 8 days of camping\, hiking\, swimming\, and padd
 ling fun. Stand tall at the edge of the world\, ride the rapids\, cycle a 
 historic former railway line\, and discover sunken shipwrecks aboard a gla
 ss bottom boat. You’ll never look at Ontario the same way again.\nNo gue
 st preparation is needed\, no equipment\, not even a sleeping bag/pad. Lak
 e Fever offers travelers free transportation\, camp-cooked meals\, and goo
 d old fashioned campfires\, but *please be advised\, on this particular to
 ur guests will be expected to share in cooking/dishes duties at least once
 .* Sightseers can enjoy access to the Canadian wilderness for a unique opp
 ortunity that would otherwise take a lot of planning and money to arrange 
 (not to worry\, first-timers will learn the basics of camping).\nThe "Buck
 et Lister" tour visits Algonquin\, Sandbanks\, Bon Echo\, and Six Mile Lak
 e Provincial Parks\, as well as Bruce Peninsula National Park\, Fathom Fiv
 e National Marine Park\, and Elora Gorge Conservation Area. Includes campi
 ng (gear and all)\, lake canoeing\, wine tasting\, many breathtaking hikes
 \, cycling\, a glass-bottom boat tour (to shipwrecks and Flower Pot Island
 )\, tubing through a limestone gorge\, and a visit to The Big Apple.\nCros
 s the great Canadian road trip off your bucket list. Who knows\, it may be
  your once-in-a-lifetime experience.\nVisit www.lakefeverwilderness.ca/the
 -bucketlister-tour for itinerary and more details.
LOCATION:Multiple Venues
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/bucket-lister-8-day-annual-camping-road-
 trip-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Christopher Titus - Doomed to Repeat
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T203000
UID:blogto-232652@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/03/24/original_imagef07898a6-6dd9-4bc7-a38f-438cee57e9
 0d.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Christopher Titus is currently touring his new show\, Doomed t
 o Repeat to sold-out audiences at clubs and theaters across the North Amer
 ica. With a take-no-prisoners wit and years of experience writing hilariou
 sly edgy and poignant comedy\, Christopher Titus is a voice unlike any oth
 er.\nChristopher has written and starred in ten 90-minute comedy specials\
 , with several spending months on the Billboard Top 10 comedy chart.  He r
 ecently released his tenth special\, Carrying Monsters\, a bookend compani
 on piece to Norman Rockwell is Bleeding (his very first show and the sourc
 e material for the Fox series).  His podcast\, The Armageddon Update/Titus
  Podcasthas over 10 million downloads.  During the worst days of the pande
 mic\, he used his self-owned studio as a safe space to exec produce and di
 rect specials for Ron Funches\, Fortune Feimster and Everlast.\n#comedy #s
 tandup
LOCATION:The Terminal Theatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/christopher-titus-doomed-to-repeat-toron
 to/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Luge LP release with So Perfect and Bag
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T235900
UID:blogto-233430@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/10/original_imagef12f345f-134e-464d-8e56-3c211c3783
 23.jpg
DESCRIPTION:LUGE\nSince 2015 Toronto’s Luge have been cutting their teet
 h into faceted gems that gnaw all inspiration into a moldable paste. Years
  of perpetual boil have combined the best of Noise Rock\, Pop\, Metal\, Fu
 nk and so many other lodes into the Mixture. No ingredient is immune to th
 e unifying power of Luge as at the crown of their arch sits a keystone ins
 cribed: It’s all just Music.\nYou cannot expect the unexpected. But Luge
  can. Luca Caruso-Moro’s drumming delivers a full-body itch to groove an
 d fight. Meanwhile Cameron Fraser brings Bassline after capital-B-Bassline
 . Tobias Hart’s guitar is the grease that threatens to break the emulsio
 n before brandishing a hook that stirs it back to safety. Kaiva Gotham’s
  keys are timeless but for their rhythm. Her voice is singular\, to say no
 thing of its variety. And her lyrics remain\, while deeply idiosyncratic\,
  equally stirring. Together Luge balances a deep misunderstanding. Each me
 mber\, patiently normal\, gives context to the others until it is their tu
 rn to be in need of translation.\nLuge celebrates the release of their lat
 est project “make miarklez irlz”\, 2 six song EPs “make” & “irlz
 ” that merge into a single twelve track album\, “miarklez” for three
  unique listening experiences. Choose your fighter & see them do it all li
 ve!\nSO PERFECT\nToronto rock quartet So Perfect formed in January of 2023
  and have been consistently gigging and recording since their inception. T
 heir new EP titled “Go Figure” showcases the band’s optimism for gro
 wth and ability to take risks while remaining true to itself. So Perfect a
 re known for being an energetic live band that is happy to stand out and w
 ill have you leaving the show humming their new song.\nBAG\nBag is a Toron
 to band that started during the Covid 19 outbreak. The members have been i
 n other music projects like Still Boys\, Wet Dirt\, and Rozasia. They soun
 d sort of like the Butthole Surfers and the Monkees.\n$20 Adv / $50 with L
 P / $25 Door\nAl Ages\nPoster by Robert Voy
LOCATION:Wavelength @ St. Anne's Parish Hall
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/luge-lp-release-with-so-perfect-and-bag-
 toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
