BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Indigenous Beading Workshop: Strawberry Patch
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T130000
UID:blogto-232271@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/03/17/original_image98567ccf-13cf-421a-bdc0-a2dd33b7ec
 14.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate National Indigenous History Month during the Strawbe
 rry Moon with a hands-on beaded otêhimin (Cree for strawberry\, often cal
 led “heartberry”) patch workshop led by Cree-Métis artist Marissa Mag
 neson. Participants will learn about the cultural and seasonal significanc
 e of the strawberry while being guided through the fundamentals of one and
 /or two-needle bead embroidery techniques. Welcoming both beginner and int
 ermediate beaders\, this workshop builds confidence and skill as you creat
 e a beautiful\, meaningful piece rooted in story and tradition.\nWhat to E
 xpect\n- Hands-on learning: Work with beads\, needles\, and thread under M
 arissa’s expert guidance\n- Cultural context: Understand the significanc
 e of beadwork in Indigenous communities and its continuing importance toda
 y\n- All materials provided: Everything you need is included—just bring 
 your creativity and curiosity\n- Welcoming atmosphere: Both beginner and i
 ntermediate beaders are welcome.
LOCATION:Bata Shoe Museum
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/indigenous-beading-workshop-strawberry-p
 atch-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
