BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Anga's Farm: Open Terrarium Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T170000
UID:blogto-233738@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/16/original_image42443230-7052-4782-9a0a-475bbdb36e
 c0.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Workshop: Open Terrarium Creation | Build Your Own Mini Jungle
 \nCreate your own miniature world of green! In this hands-on workshop\, yo
 u’ll design and build a beautiful open terrarium set in a modern glass v
 essel with a natural wooden base.\nYou’ll be guided step-by-step through
  the entire process\, from layering different soils and drainage materials
  to selecting and arranging your plants. Using a mix of decorative rocks\,
  moss\, and natural accents\, you’ll create a unique piece that fits you
 r style.\nParticipants will:\nCreate their own open terrarium using a sele
 ction of tropical plants\nLearn how to properly layer soil\, drainage\, an
 d decorative elements\nExplore different design styles using rocks\, moss\
 , and natural textures\nGain simple\, practical care tips to keep their te
 rrarium healthy and thriving\nEvery terrarium is unique\, and you’ll hav
 e the freedom to make it your own\, whether you prefer something lush and 
 full or clean and minimal. By the end of the session\, you’ll take home 
 a beautiful\, low-maintenance indoor garden—perfect for brightening your
  space or gifting to someone special. This workshop is beginner-friendly a
 nd a fun\, creative way to spend time with plants.\nVisit our website for 
 more details & to sign up! www.angasfarm.ca
LOCATION:Anga's Farm & Nursery
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/angas-farm-open-terrarium-workshop-toron
 to/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
